  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expert Support Platform for Resilience  (ESPRE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The creation of a dedicated Expert Support Platform for Resilience (ESPRE) is key to ensure that thematic support on resilience, conflict sensitivity and HDP nexus is timely and swiftly delivered, complementing the expertise and capacities in the EU Delegations and in Headquarters. ESPRE will be formed by a pool of experts providing methodological and thematic support on (1) the three main components of the HDP nexus, (2) on the six dimensions of fragility (economic, environmental, human, political, security and societal), and (3) on conflict sensitivity in programming. This facility will make it possible to mobilise relevant expertise within a short notice and following a simple pre-established procedure (hence considerably reducing bureaucratic burdens). The duration of the assignments will be flexible (from two weeks to approximately six months) and will depend on the nature and scale of the needs of the EU delegation, strategic considerations and specific aspects of fragility and dimensions.</narrative>
  </description>
